<title>CHILE: LAN Chile says buys Boeing jets for $300 mln.</title>
<headline>LAN Chile says buys Boeing jets for $300 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean airline LAN Chile has signed a contract to purchase three new Boeing 767-300 ER jets for $300 million and has also taken out an option to buy two more of the same sort of aircraft in 1999, LAN President Jorge Awad said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the biggest direct purchase in the history of Chilean civil aviation and it is also the biggest made in the past few years by a Latin American airline, which tend to operate leased fleets,&quot; Awad said.</p>
<p>He said LAN would finance the deal with a credit for a period of about 12 years from the Canadian International Investment Bank.</p>
<p>((--Gabriela Donoso, Santiago Newsroom +562 6995595 x205)).</p>
